    <node id="Recon-All">
      <data key="d0">Recon-All</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A software tool that processes brain imaging data, capable of resampling data onto an average subject and smoothing it at various FWHM values when run with the -qcache option.&lt;SEP&gt;A processing workflow used in FreeSurfer for cross-sectional and longitudinal analysis of neuroimaging data.</data>
      <data key="d3">SBM_CACHE-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;LONG-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">SBM_CACHE&lt;SEP&gt;LONG</data>
      <data key="d5">1792427144</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fsaverage">
      <data key="d0">Fsaverage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The average subject template used by recon-all for resampling data during qcache processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">SBM_CACHE-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">SBM_CACHE</data>
      <data key="d5">1792427114</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="FWHM">
      <data key="d0">FWHM</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Full-width/half-max values, typically 0, 5, 10, 15, 20, and 25mm, used for smoothing data in the qcache processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Full Width at Half Maximum, a measure of the width of a smoothing kernel used in image processing, with values ranging from 4.6mm to 9mm in the context.</data>
      <data key="d3">SBM_CACHE-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;VBM_FINAL-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">SBM_CACHE&lt;SEP&gt;VBM_FINAL</data>
      <data key="d5">1792428582</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Qcache">
      <data key="d0">Qcache</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An option in recon-all that resamples data onto the average subject and smooths it at various FWHM values, caching the results to speed later processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">SBM_CACHE-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">SBM_CACHE</data>
      <data key="d5">1792427114</data>
      <data key="d6" />
