    <node id="run_full_pipeline.sh">
      <data key="d0">run_full_pipeline.sh</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A shell script that can be executed with the -h flag to display full usage notes and additional examples.&lt;SEP&gt;A shell script that serves as the wrapper for the PREEMACS pipeline. It validates command-line arguments, checks for required files, and invokes the pipeline.&lt;SEP&gt;A shell script in the PREEMACS repository that contains the resolve_modality_binds function implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">NHP_WRAPPER-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;WRAPPER_LICENSE-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;WRAPPER_BINDS-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">NHP_WRAPPER&lt;SEP&gt;WRAPPER_LICENSE&lt;SEP&gt;WRAPPER_BINDS</data>
      <data key="d5">1792428673</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Randomise">
      <data key="d0">Randomise</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A software tool that allows the definition of exchangeability blocks for permutation tests, as specified by the group_labels option, to accommodate repeated measures in multisubject analyses.&lt;SEP&gt;A software tool that runs permutation-based non-parametric inference, generating tstat maps and p-value maps.&lt;SEP&gt;A nonparametric permutation testing tool within FSL for statistical analysis of neuroimaging data, used for one-sample t-tests.&lt;SEP&gt;A tool that performs permutation-based inference, automatically selecting one-sample mode for appropriate design/contrast combinations.&lt;SEP&gt;A command in FSL used to run permutation-based inference, invoked with options -i PairedT4D -o PairedT -d design.mat -t design.con -e design.grp -m mask -T.</data>
      <data key="d3">STAT_BLOCK-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;VBM_FINAL-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;STAT_ONEGROUP-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;STAT_ONEGROUP-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;STAT_PAIRED-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">STAT_BLOCK&lt;SEP&gt;VBM_FINAL&lt;SEP&gt;STAT_ONEGROUP&lt;SEP&gt;STAT_PAIRED</data>
      <data key="d5">1792428629</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Permutation Tests">
      <data key="d0">Permutation Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Statistical tests that do not easily accommodate correlated datasets because such dependence violates null-hypothesis exchangeability.</data>
      <data key="d3">STAT_BLOCK-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">STAT_BLOCK</data>
      <data key="d5">1792427122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Exchangeability Blocks">
      <data key="d0">Exchangeability Blocks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Groups defined by the group_labels option in randomise, within which observations are permuted; only observations with the same group label are exchanged.</data>
      <data key="d3">STAT_BLOCK-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">STAT_BLOCK</data>
      <data key="d5">1792427122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Group Labels">
      <data key="d0">Group Labels</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Labels specified via the group_labels option that define exchangeability blocks for permutation in randomise.</data>
      <data key="d3">STAT_BLOCK-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">STAT_BLOCK</data>
      <data key="d5">1792427122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Repeated Measures">
      <data key="d0">Repeated Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A case in multisubject analysis where there is more than one measurement per subject, which can sometimes be accommodated by permutation tests using exchangeability blocks.</data>
      <data key="d3">STAT_BLOCK-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">STAT_BLOCK</data>
      <data key="d5">1792427122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Null-Hypothesis Exchangeability">
      <data key="d0">Null-Hypothesis Exchangeability</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A principle in permutation testing that is violated by correlated datasets, such as temporally smooth timeseries.</data>
      <data key="d3">STAT_BLOCK-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">STAT_BLOCK</data>
      <data key="d5">1792427122</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Guide">
      <data key="d0">Guide</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A document referenced in the source that contains a repeated measures example for more detail.</data>
